"{\"reasoning\":\"GBW requires gm1\u22482\u03c0\u00b750MHz\u00b71pF=0.314mS. To obtain phase margin \u226560\u00b0, mirror pole must be \u2265\u224887MHz, so increase gm3\u22480.55mS by raising tail current. Using gm/Id=10 for all devices gives Id\u224855\u00b5A per input transistor, tail current Itail\u2248110\u00b5A. Power=3.3V\u00b72\u00b7110\u00b5A\u2248726\u00b5W<1mW. With L=0.5\u00b5m, NMOS gm/gds\u2248174, PMOS gm/gds\u2248261, yielding gds2\u22483.2\u00b5S, gds4\u22482.1\u00b5S, total\u22485.3\u00b5S, so A0\u22480.55mS/5.3\u00b5S\u2248104\u224840dB>35dB. Output swing \u2248VDD\u2011Vov\u2011(Vtail+Vov)\u22483.3\u20110.2\u20110.4\u22482.7V>1.5V. All specs met.\",\"gmid1\":10,\"L1_um\":0.5,\"gmid3\":10,\"L3_um\":0.5,\"gmid5\":10,\"L5_um\":0.5,\"Itail_uA\":110}"